.TH "ROARK\-CALL\-PROPERTY\-UPDATE" "1" "" "roark-call-property-update" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-call\-property\-update \- Update the properties of a call
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark call property update
\fIcall\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Add, overwrite or remove custom properties on an already\-existing call. Use this for data that becomes available after the call was created, e.g. an outcome your system validates a few minutes later. Merge semantics: a value adds or overwrites the property, null removes it, and properties left out are untouched. The patch is applied whole or not at all: a property Roark sets itself, or a value whose type differs from the type the project already stores that property as, rejects the request with a 400 and nothing is written. A 409 means another request created one of the properties with a different value type at the same moment; nothing was written. Optionally pass `metrics` to (re)score metrics over the updated properties, which triggers a billed metric collection job and requires the `metric:create` permission.
.SH "API"
PATCH /v1/call/{callId}/properties
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIcall\-id\fR
The call\-id.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-properties\fR \fI<value>\fR
Properties to change on the call. A string, number or boolean value adds the property or overwrites it; null removes it. Properties left out are untouched. Keys are stored in snake_case, as on POST /v1/call. A property keeps the value type it was first stored with in the project, so a value of another type is rejected. Properties Roark sets itself (direction, duration_seconds, agent_id, ...) can't be changed. Max 100 per request. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-metrics\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional. Metric definitions to (re)score on this call once the properties are written, e.g. metrics that read the call's properties. Triggers a metric collection job (billed, credit\-gated) and requires the 'metric:create' permission. Omit to update properties without scoring. Max 20. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark call property update <call\-id> \-\-properties <value>
.fi
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
